From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:41:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make the menus fit a handheld console

- Prompts ask for the A and B buttons instead of the Y and N keys, and
  yes/no prompts also accept Enter and Backspace, which the buttons send.
- Savegames are named after the level, eg. "E1M3: Toxin Refinery",
  without asking for a name, there is no keyboard to type one.
- Without writable storage, like a Nintendo DS without an SD card,
  saving ended the game with an I_Error. Save Game and Quick Save now
  check first and show a message, so you can keep playing.
- The main menu has Options below Save Game, and its last item is End
  Game while playing and Quit Game otherwise. No Read This! (keyboard
  help), and Options only has Messages and Sound Volume: there is no
  keyboard or mouse, and the view always fills the top screen at its
  resolution, so no graphic detail, screen size or mouse sensitivity.
- Sound and music start at full volume, the DS speakers are small. The
  sliders set the balance, the hardware volume control the loudness.
---
